<title>LEBANON: Lebanon imported $769 mln of oil products in 1996.</title>
<headline>Lebanon imported $769 mln of oil products in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's 1996 imports of oil products rose to 4.3 million tonnes and cost $769 million, oil ministry figures issued on Monday showed.</p>
<p>This compared with 4.08 million tonnes imported at a cost of $630 million in 1995.</p>
<p>The ministry issued the following figures (in thousands of tonnes, millions of dollars, 1995 figures in brackets):</p>
<p>			     Quantity		Cost</p>
<p>    - Petrol	   1,380 (1,350)     290.9 (240.9)</p>
<p>    - Diesel fuel	930 (1,010)     184.5 (159.0)</p>
<p>    - Fuel oil	 1,620 (1,430)     216.6 (168.5)</p>
<p>    - Jet fuel	   106   (109)	23.5  (19.9)</p>
<p>    - Liquid gas	 123   (121)	37.3  (33.0)</p>
<p>    - Asphalt	    108    (68)	16.3   (8.5)</p>
<p>-- Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307 745308</p>
</text>
